    "updated_at": "2016-05-20T13:58:04Z",
    "body": "Actually, there is a practical implication to this conflation of repeated timers and nesting:\n\n``` js\nx = 0;\nsetInterval(function() {\n  x++;\n  if (x == 5) {\n    setTimeout(function() { ... }, 0);\n  }\n}, 1000);\n```\n\nIt's counterintuitive to me that the setTimeout is expected to be clamped to a minimum time greater than 0, given the specification text.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
