    "created_at": "2016-05-20T14:51:52Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-05-20T14:52:04Z",
    "body": "If the behaviour that's written is intentional, which it appears to be, I don't have any clear suggestions. My initial reading struck me as a possible oversight given the conflation between nesting and non-nested behaviours. If we either rename the things related to nesting to encompass repeating timers as well, or add a note explaining that repeated timers are intentionally treated equivalently to nested ones, that would satisfy me.\n",
